{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And she could no longer hide him.</b> For the Egyptians had appointed over her [guards] from the day she took him back, and she bore him at six months and one day (ibid.) — for one who gives birth at seven [months] can give birth at fractional [intervals] (Niddah 38) — and they checked after her at the end of nine [months]." "<b>Gome.</b> גְּמִי in Mishnaic language (Shabbat 78), and in לַעַז יונק\"ו, and it is a soft thing and withstands both soft and hard (Sotah 12)." "<b>With clay and with pitch.</b> Pitch on the outside and clay on the inside, so that that righteous man would not smell the foul odor of pitch (ibid.)." "<b>And she placed it in the reeds.</b> It is the term for a marsh, רושיי\"ל בְּלַעַז, and similar to it: ״קָנֶה וָסוּף קָמֵלוּ״ (Isaiah 19)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French jonc, 'reed/bulrush'", 3 "the la'az is Old French ros(i)el or rosel, 'reed-bed/marsh'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:10.300654589Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}